{
 "schema": "sar.r1.stages.v1",
 "job": "j1b",
 "complete": true,
 "note": "J1b = the robustness run on config M (W2-TJ1B: F19, N8, N5, F6). Launch with --pull r1/runs/<last j1a>/stages/=/work/j1a_stages/ (a resumed J1a re-pushes its skipped stages, so the set is complete). restore_j1a lays the J1a products out under /work/j1a, digest-checked against each J1a .done.json (config/r1/layouts/j1b_from_j1a.json), and keeps the J1a markers in its own output so every reader's fingerprint follows J1a. rob_jobs builds the unit list; par_plan (N8) plans PAR x threads and STOPs above 450 GiB; each run_units group stage first checks the plan's split_after: a group of launch 2 stops launch 1 (SPLIT_STOP, rc 5) until the split group's marker is in $SAR_RESUME_DIR, so J1b runs as two launches joined by --resume-from (R11). No rob_controls stage: controls run inside their cells' group (R1P3-29). Star departure (F20) is out of scope: author 2026-10-15, the paper prints no star-departure robustness. W3-FLIPS sets complete after the cross-model review.",
 "stages": [
  {
   "name": "verify_inputs",
   "owner": "F25",
   "script": "pipeline/aws/r1/verify_inputs.py",
   "cmd": "\"$PY\" \"$WORK/verify_inputs.py\" data --job-spec \"$REPO_DIR/config/r1/jobs/j1b.json\" --pins \"$REPO_DIR/config/r1/input_pins.json\" --out \"$STAGE_OUT\"",
   "inputs": [
    "repo:config/r1/jobs/j1b.json",
    "repo:config/r1/input_pins.json"
   ],
   "outputs": [
    "work:prod/verify_inputs"
   ],
   "est_min": 10,
   "needs": [],
   "resume": "always"
  },
  {
   "name": "config",
